Subject: [PATCH] wallet(v2): build legacy version 2 transactions explicitly

CWallet holds legacy coins and signs them with legacy signatures, so its
transactions are legacy version 2. Set the version explicitly instead of
relying on CMutableTransaction's default.

The migratetov2 RPC of the design (sweeping legacy P2PKH/P2SH coins into a
v7 transaction through bridge signatures) is deferred: it needs a C++
bridge signature creator, V2 output construction and fee estimation for
bridge witnesses in the legacy wallet, which is larger than this
workstream's minimal wallet scope (Q7).

Test: wallet_tests/wallet_creates_legacy_v2_transactions.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
Preserve earlier purposeful source repairs through downstream consumer/context adaptations; exact conflict ledger retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.

Coordinator causal payout integration (2026-10-20):
Original2b12a501 wallet ownership remains tracked but native outputs are not advertised spendable/solvable by ordinary legacy-only funder/signer. Native wallet signing is separate. Combined runtime NOT_RUN.

